                <pb facs="0991" n="841" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg841"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7666/9.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister for
                        Foreign Affairs of Mexico.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I thank Your Excellency for your telegram 14th instant, inviting the Government
                    of the United States in name Mexican Government to send a delegate to the third
                    international sanitary convention to meet at Mexico City December 2. Invitation
                    so courteously extended will have prompt consideration, and I shall have the
                    honor to answer definitely in a few days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
